highlight.js (BSD-3-Clause) — bundled locally with esbuild.

This file (highlight.min.js) is a custom, minified build containing the
highlight.js core engine plus ten language grammars this site's docs and
code samples actually use: bash, go, sql, json, yaml, html (xml), javascript,
nginx (also used for Caddyfile — highlight.js has no dedicated Caddy grammar,
and nginx's directive/block/string/comment shapes are the nearest fit),
ini/toml, and plaintext as a safe fallback for an unrecognised or unlabeled
fence. No other language grammars are included. Built from the highlight.js
npm package; nothing is fetched from a CDN at runtime.

